==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lang=la|custodia||a keeping, watch, guard, prison}}, from {{term|lang=la|custos||a keeper, watchman, guard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkʌstədiː/}} ([[w:Estuary English|Estuary English]])
* {{homophones|lang=en|custardy}} (in some dialects)

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-}}

# The legal right to take care of something or somebody, especially children.
#: ''The court awarded '''custody''' to the child's father.''
# Temporary [[possession]] or care of somebody else's property.
#: ''I couldn't pay the bill and now my passport is in '''custody''' of the hotel management.''
# The state of being imprisoned or detained, usually pending a [[trial]].
#: ''He was mistreated while in police '''custody'''.''

